---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="Comic Strip Canvas privacy policy. How we collect, use, and protect your personal data."
>
  <section class="relative bg-panel-dark py-16">
    <div class="absolute top-0 left-0 right-0 h-1 bg-comic-red"></div>
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <nav class="flex items-center gap-2 font-source text-sm text-gray-500 mb-6">
        <a href="/" class="hover:text-comic-yellow transition-colors">Home</a>
        <span>/</span>
        <span class="text-off-white">Privacy Policy</span>
      </nav>
      <h1 class="font-bangers text-5xl text-off-white tracking-wide mb-4" style="text-shadow: 3px 3px 0 rgba(0,0,0,0.4);">PRIVACY POLICY</h1>
      <p class="font-source text-gray-400 text-sm">Last updated: 4 October 2026</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12">
    <div class="space-y-8 font-source text-gray-300 text-sm leading-relaxed">
      <div>
        <h2 class="font-russo text-off-white text-lg uppercase tracking-wide mb-3">Who We Are</h2>
        <p>Comic Strip Canvas is a UK-based wall art brand. Our website address is https://comicstripcanvas.co.uk. We are committed to protecting your privacy and handling your personal data responsibly.</p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-russo text-off-white text-lg uppercase tracking-wide mb-3">What Data We Collect</h2>
        <p class="mb-3">When you place an order or contact us, we may collect the following information:</p>
        <p>Your name, email address, shipping address, phone number (if provided), payment information (processed securely by Stripe — we do not store card details), photographs you upload for personalised orders, and any messages or instructions you provide. If you accept analytics cookies, we also collect information about how you use our site (see Cookies below).</p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-russo text-off-white text-lg uppercase tracking-wide mb-3">How We Use Your Data</h2>
        <p>We use your personal data to process and fulfil your orders, send order confirmations and dispatch notifications, create personalised artwork based on photos you provide, respond to your enquiries, improve our website and services, and send marketing emails (only if you've opted in via our newsletter). We will never sell your personal data to third parties.</p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-russo text-off-white text-lg uppercase tracking-wide mb-3">Payment Processing</h2>
        <p>All payments are processed securely through Stripe. We do not store or have access to your full card details. Stripe's privacy policy can be found at stripe.com/privacy.</p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-russo text-off-white text-lg uppercase tracking-wide mb-3">Photos & Personalised Orders</h2>
        <p>When you upload photos for personalised orders, these are stored securely and used solely for the purpose of creating your artwork. We will never use your photos for marketing without your explicit consent.</p>
        <p class="mt-3">We keep your photos and the finished artwork for 90 days after dispatch in case a reprint is needed, then delete them. If you start a personalised build but do not order, the photos you uploaded are deleted 30 days after you started it.</p>
        <p class="mt-3">To apply the comic style, your photo is sent to Google's Gemini API, acting as our data processor. We send the photo you uploaded together with three reference images of our own artwork, which is how the style is matched. We use Google's paid API tier, under which Google does not use the data you send to train its models.</p>
        <p class="mt-3">For the comic book cover, background removal runs on our own service hosted on Fly.io in London; the image is not retained by that service.</p>
        <p class="mt-3">The styled image comes back to us and is stored in our own Netlify Blobs store alongside your original photo, under the same retention rules: 90 days after dispatch, or 30 days if you start a build and do not order.</p>
        <p class="mt-3">Before your first upload you are asked to confirm that you own the rights to the photos, or have permission to use them, and that you are happy for us to use them to make your artwork.</p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-russo text-off-white text-lg uppercase tracking-wide mb-3">Cookies</h2>
        <p><strong class="text-off-white">Essential storage (always on).</strong> Some storage is needed for the site to work, so it does not need your consent: your basket (kept in your browser's local storage), your cookie choice itself (a cookie called <code>csc_consent</code>, kept for 6 months), and the security cookies set by Stripe on its secure checkout page and by Cloudflare Turnstile, which protects our contact form from spam.</p>
        <p class="mt-3"><strong class="text-off-white">Analytics (only with your consent).</strong> We use Google Analytics 4 (measurement ID G-LH10709LC0), loaded directly from Google, to measure visits to the site and the steps of shopping: viewing a product, adding to your bag, starting checkout and completing a purchase. Google Analytics only runs after you click "Accept all" on our cookie banner, and only for analytics: advertising storage and ad personalisation stay switched off. If you click "Reject all", or make no choice, it does not load and no analytics cookies are set. When they do run, Google Analytics sets cookies called <code>_ga</code> and <code>_ga_&lt;ID&gt;</code>, and Google receives information such as the pages you visit, your device and browser, and an approximate location derived from your IP address. Google's privacy policy is at policies.google.com/privacy.</p>
        <p class="mt-3"><strong class="text-off-white">Purchases.</strong> If you accepted analytics, your browser passes your Google Analytics IDs (the random identifiers Google Analytics gives your browser and your visit, from the <code>_ga</code> cookies) to our checkout. When you pay, our server sends Google those IDs with your order number, the order value, postage and the items bought, so the purchase appears in our analytics. Nothing that identifies you personally, such as your name, email or address, is sent. If you did not accept, nothing is sent.</p>
        <p class="mt-3"><strong class="text-off-white">Changing your choice.</strong> You can change your mind at any time using the "Cookie Settings" link at the bottom of every page. If you withdraw consent, we delete the analytics cookies set on our domain and the tags stop loading from your next page view. We ask again after 6 months.</p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-russo text-off-white text-lg uppercase tracking-wide mb-3">Your Rights</h2>
        <p>Under UK GDPR, you have the right to access the personal data we hold about you, request correction or deletion of your data, object to processing of your data, and request a copy of your data in a portable format. To exercise any of these rights, please contact us via our contact page.</p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-russo text-off-white text-lg uppercase tracking-wide mb-3">Contact</h2>
        <p>For any privacy-related questions, please <a href="/contact/" class="text-comic-cyan hover:text-comic-yellow transition-colors">contact us</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
